Equivalent inductance of inductances connected in parallel is $\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{p}}=\frac{1}{\mathrm{~L}_1}+\frac{1}{\mathrm{~L}_2}\therefore \quad \mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{p}}=\frac{1}{\left(\frac{2}{\mathrm{~L}}+\frac{2}{\mathrm{~L}}\right)}=\frac{\mathrm{L}}{4}$<br/>Equivalent inductance in series
$\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{s}} & =\mathrm{L}_{\mathrm{p}}+\mathrm{L}_3 \\
& =\frac{\mathrm{L}}{4}+\frac{3}{4} \mathrm{~L}=\mathrm{L}
